    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0375" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/2200¾</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose a confidential
                    telegram received from Ambassador Page at London,<anchor n="93" xml:id="d269-f1"
                    /> which was decoded yesterday. The telegram was in the private cipher and is
                    more or less garbled—however, <pb facs="0376" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/> I think
                    that it is sufficiently clear in expressing Mr. Page’s view as to the present
                    situation.</p>
                <p>I give more weight to the telegram because he had, at the time of sending it, had
                    the advantage of consultation with Colonel House. Possibly you have received
                    from Colonel House telegrams which will throw light on Mr. Page’s point of view
                    and also that of the British Government. I hope that you will have had this
                    called to your attention before determining what course we should take with
                    regard to Germany.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
